  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Trade and Investment activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Central America Regional):  The new Regional Trade and Investment activity will strengthen digitization of trade processes, improve trade policies, modernize regulations, improve private sector export competitiveness, and spur regional investments and access to finance, including in clean energy. The activity will establish a permanent academy to train regional border officials, the private sector, trade and logistics operators, and other trade stakeholders on the Dominican Republic-Central America Free Trade Agreement, best practices in trade facilitation, and coordinated border management. It will improve information technology linkages across border agencies, promote transparency, predictability, and efficiency of trade processes, and create opportunities for companies to access international markets. The activity will support businesses to comply with international trade processes and standards by increasing the number of Authorized Economic Operators. This holistic approach makes this activity best suited to support regional trade integration.The activity will attract investment for regional initiatives, including cross-border logistics, transport, and trade finance to make regional value chains more competitive. It will identify and address key investment constraints, offering advisory services, feasibility studies, blended finance, financial structuring, market linkages, and other support to reduce investment risks. To boost renewable energy investments, the activity will forge regional partnerships with renewable energy project developers, energy utilities, energy services companies, and battery storage manufacturers, accelerating the adoption of renewable energy and energy efficiency technologies.</narrative>
  </description>
